{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792774495,"nonce":"k7mTj/V9l7L9juZf92kgCKRK6Fc=","title":"Compiler: field access on a block expression with control flow reads the field before the block's value exists","message":"When the object of a `TypedExpression::Field` is a `TypedExpression::Block` whose statements branch (an `if` before the final value), SSA emits the field's `gep` and `load` in the block where the object expression started, ahead of the continuation block that defines the object value. The interpreter then reads an undefined operand: `Execution error: type mismatch: expected pointer, got Undef`.\n\nThe TypeScript frontend produces this shape for a field read on an array element whose index is not proven in bounds: the element read is a block that tests the index, calls `$TS$index_trap` on failure, then reads the element. Present at HEAD f5b00ff1, independent of uncommitted work. It now also blocks module arrays of class instances (git-bug 751af73), since reads of a module global carry no bounds facts.\n\nReproducer (committed frontend; /private/tmp/zynode-ts-head is a frozen HEAD build):\n\n    /private/tmp/zynode-ts-head run /private/tmp/ts-field-block-repro/field_of_checked_index.ts\n\n    class Point { x: number = 0; }\n    function first(ps: Point[]): number { return ps[0].x; }\n    const pts: Point[] = [new Point()];\n    console.log(first(pts));\n\nExpected `0`; actual exit 4 with the error above, in the interpreter (the first tier, so `--llvm` shows it too). HIR: /private/tmp/ts-field-block-repro/hir, function `fn$first`: `%v11: u8 = gep %v12, [%v4]` and `%v14 = load %v13` sit in block0 while `%v12` is defined in block3, the join after the bounds test.","files":null}]}